<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khmer Rouge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1960s–<a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Communist Party of Kampuchea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge was the name given to the Communist Party of Kampuchea and its armed forces. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pol-pot">Pol Pot</a>, it fought the Khmer Republic, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> in April 1975 and ruled as Democratic Kampuchea, emptying the cities and causing the deaths of around 1.5 to 2 million people through execution, forced labour and famine. Overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in 1979, it fought on from the Thai border until its collapse in the late 1990s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge.jpg" alt="Khmer Rouge" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This (SVG on base of source) was created by me. See File History, below, for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Democratic_Kampuchea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
